  "finalText": "I built the **Bloom** logo sting at 6 s, 1920×1080, 60 fps, with a cream background (#f6efe0) and deep green ink (#1f4d3a). I checked it with one contact sheet, but I didn't run the critic or a second tweak round.\n\n- **Lead-in (0–0.4 s):** a still cream frame.\n- **Write (0.4–3 s):** the **bloom wordmark** is a single monoline script path that draws itself on in one continuous stroke, easing in and out (Sine In Out).\n- **Leaf (2.9–3.9 s):** the **leaf** is a solid green shape above the second \"o\". It grows from its base with a small overshoot and settle.\n- **Hold (3.9–6 s):** the finished lockup stays still.\n\nThe script is hand-built from curves, so the \"b\" bowl reads a little like an \"l\". The lockup also sits slightly right of the canvas centre.\n\nI can redraw the \"b\", centre the lockup, or move the leaf over the first \"o\" if you want."
